Lab: Azure Interface

Objective

Configure Azure by creating a Resource Group.

Environment

Tools Used

Microsoft Azure Portal
Azure Resource Groups
Azure Subscription Management

Operating System

Microsoft Azure

Skills Practiced

Cloud Administration
Resource Management
Azure Portal Navigation
Cloud Infrastructure Configuration

Actions Performed

1. Logged into MS Azure Portal.
2. Under Navigate, clicked on the Resource groups option.
3. The new page shows no resource groups. Clicked on Create Resource Group.
4. In the Project details, I clicked on the appropriate subscription and provided a Resource group name
5. Under the Resource details in Region, I selected the appropriate Region for the clients utilizing the Resource Group
6. I reviewed the setting for accuracy and created the Group.
7. Documented findings and ended lab

Commands Used

None

Verification

After reviewing, Microsoft Azure opened into a new page containing the Resource Group created under the Subscription. 

Issues Encountered

None

Resolution

Successfully created and verified the Azure Resource Group within the selected subscription and region. 
Confirmed the Resource Group was available for future cloud resource deployments. 

Key Takeaways

Created and configured an Azure Resource Group to logically organize and manage cloud resources within a subscription. 
I learned that Resource Groups serve as containers for Azure services, such as virtual machines, storage accounts, 
and networking resources. 

